 # Tailscale
@@ -22,6 +14,28 @@ Tailscale is a zero-config mesh VPN that creates a secure peer-to-peer network (

 Beyond the core VPN, Tailscale offers a family of products built on the same identity and networking layer. This skill covers all of them — consult the reference file for whichever topic is relevant.

+## Fleet integration
+
+On fleet-managed machines, read the `fleet` skill for machine discovery,
+installation ownership, and local operating rules. Tailscale remains an
+OS-managed service. Keep the fleet's artifact publishing route; the Serve and
+Funnel examples below do not override it. Use the installed CLI help and
+current official documentation to verify changing flags and policy syntax.
+
+Use the fleet manifest for persistent user-level CLI tools, then push and
+converge with the fleet sync script. Never install them globally by hand.
+For one-off helper tools, use `pixi exec --spec <package> <command>` (for
+example, `pixi exec --spec jq jq --version`). For project work, declare the
+toolchain and dependencies in `pixi.toml` and run commands with `pixi run`.
+Do not use pip, uv, npm, or Go commands to install global tools. Native
+services such as Tailscale and Docker remain OS-managed, not Pixi packages.
+
+Check `tailscale version` and service status before using installation
+examples. On an existing fleet host, use its OS package/update workflow;
+the bootstrap examples are for new, unmanaged hosts. Keep secrets out of
+repositories and synced configuration; use the fleet's machine-local
+`~/.secrets.env` or the CI secret store.
+
